From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:47:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sources: pin_review records the apply-count claim as WRONG,
 not disputed (checker F1, resolved against me)

I had re-run my own measurement twice, got 12/12 conflict both times, and recorded a disagreement rather than conceding. The checker proved it a THIRD time with the index state shown - ls-files -s blob d61c1c190 matching rev-parse 0347ab14a of ggml-cuda.cu, and git apply --cached --3way -v printing Applied patch cleanly - and diagnosed my harness: under --cached a conflicted path DROPS OUT of the index, so my sequential run cascaded and eight later commits failed with does-not-exist-in-index. I was measuring the cascade, not the content.

The review now says the claim was WRONG and tells future readers not to quote any apply-conflict count from this lane. The justification of record stays what it should always have been: byte-identity with the fork on backends this estate cannot build.

Taken-from: TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant@7ebcbb0b6
Origin: lane-154 checker finding F1 (HIGH), second pass.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - a pin review changes no runtime behaviour.
Lane: lane-154
---
 tools/arifi-sync/sources.json | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

