       "pin_review": "lane-110C turbokv matrix (trial-evidence/110/turbokv-matrix.json) measured this tree end-to-end; WHT non-interchangeability proven against it (RESUME finding 4). That measurement was of c26cbdffc's LINEAGE - see the lane-143 key for why the sha moved and why the claim survives.",
       "pin_review_2026_08_17_lane143": "THE OLD PIN WAS NOT MERELY BEHIND, IT WAS ON A LINEAGE THE FORK'S HEAD NEVER TOOK. c26cbdffc is 'Merge pull request #225 from TheTom/fix-ui-assets-partial-dist' (2026-07-18). `git branch -r --contains c26cbdffc` returns exactly two refs, turboquant/fix/vulkan-turbo3-flat-dequant-241 and turboquant/tom/merge-upstream-dsv4 - it is NOT contained by feature/turboquant-kv-cache, which is what origin/HEAD resolves to. merge-base(c26cbdffc, head) = 1fd6dfe9f, an UPSTREAM UI commit from 2026-06-14, and rev-list --left-right --count gives 338/841. So any 'c26cbdffc..head = 841 commits behind' figure is divergent-history arithmetic, not a delta. Re-pinned to f6124e914 (2026-08-17). The lane-110C claim above SURVIVES the move: the TurboQuant KV/WHT surface it measured is intact at the head, so this was a stale pin, not an evaporated finding. MEASURED DELTA from the merge-base: 816 non-merge, of which 151 are fork-authored (--not upstream/master) and 33 touch turbo/TQ quant or kernels; the other ~118 are upstream sync, DeepseekV4/DSpark, UI and CI. WHAT WE TAKE, ranked. (1) 7f8302613 'ggml-cpu : declare turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size extern, not a second definition' (2026-08-07) plus follow-up c7d6442dd (2026-08-12) - NO-OP FOR US, take only for tidiness. SELF-REFUTATION, recorded because this lane first wrote the opposite and the correction is the valuable part: I initially read recut's ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp:26 `GGML_API int turbo3_cpu_wht_group_size;` as a SECOND DEFINITION in libggml-cpu against the real one in ggml-turbo-quant.c:31-32, and called it a live defect on our Windows DLL build on the strength of the fix's own commit message ('ELF interposition may merge them; two-level-namespace and DLL targets will not'). THAT WAS WRONG, and the error was not expanding the macro. In recut/2026-08-16:ggml/include/ggml.h, GGML_API expands to `... extern` in ALL FOUR branches (dllexport extern / dllimport extern / visibility-default extern / bare extern), so ops.cpp:26 is a DECLARATION on every platform and every build mode, and no second definition exists anywhere in our tree. Worse for the original framing: at turboquant's own pre-fix commit 7f8302613^ only the NON-Windows branch lacked `extern` (`__attribute__((visibility(\"default\")))` with no extern), so their bug lived on ELF/macOS and their commit message has the platform exactly BACKWARDS - the Windows branches already carried extern. Our tree is correct as it stands; these two commits change nothing for us. (2) cd4c3a1f6 'remove the per-call mallocs from the TurboQuant vec_dot kernels' (CPU, pure win). (3) e130aef60 'close complete-audit findings - 7 port regressions + TQ4_1S dp4a kernel' (an audit of exactly the port we did). (4) The Vulkan cluster of 2026-08-03/04, our backend: 844678bf2 SET_ROWS block decomposition for turbo weight types, 160649054 TQ MUL_MAT_ID size gate limited to the f16 dequant fallback, 5f5ef77ad TQ4_1S pipeline wiring, 4f2013d66 turbo3 KV pipeline, b43efe599 turbo3 wiring correction, 353ac109e + 637300387 mul_mat_vec_id add / MUL_MAT_ID reject, b514ae496 TQ3_1S weight type, b0c39adac TQ4_1S wiring restored - our merge 70a752991 post-dates these so several are probably already in, and EACH needs a content diff before cherry-picking (per-commit tree comparison across a rebase is a build lane's job, not a register lane's). (5) f050a2501 + a70a324fa fattn-vec turbo-K split for a VGPR spill, re-gated on the LUT rather than on D - authored for HIP/CUDA, but the gating correction is architecture-general. WHAT WE SKIP AND WHY: 3243b2875 (fused TQ3_1S mul_mat on HIP gfx1100 - our rig is a 780M gfx1103 on Vulkan, not HIP), 8365224ee (CUDA-only garbage-output fix), ffc210bfb (arm64 CI), 07e01ec54 + ce3dce77b + aab782c1b (DeepseekV4/DSpark model support - a different slot), and the ~118 upstream-sync commits which arrive with the next upstream move. CONTRACT CHECK: CLEAN. This head defines TQ3_1S=45 and TQ4_1S=46, exactly the ids TYPE-ID-ALLOCATION.md section 3.1 reserves, so verbatim adoption still holds. Runtime types sit at 43/44/47. FLAG E, the one silent-capable collision in the whole contract, CONFIRMED AT THIS HEAD: TURBO2_0 is id 43 and our Q2_0_G128 is id 43, and block_turbo2_0 (ggml_half + qs[128/4] = 34 B / 128 values) is BYTE-IDENTICAL AND FIELD-IDENTICAL to block_q2_0_g128, so gguf_init's row-size check has nothing to separate them and the g128 metadata gate keys off a marker a turbo2 file would never carry - a serialized TURBO2_0 read as our g128 would dequantize wrongly and KEEP GOING (turbo2 is WHT-rotated Lloyd-Max, ours is plain scaled). THAT 'SILENT' VERDICT IS CODE-DERIVED, NOT CONTRACT-PROSE: read at recut/2026-08-16:src/llama-model-loader.cpp, llama_gguf_q2_0_g128_gate returns FALSE on `key < 0` (line 133-135) without throwing, and the only consumer is `if (q2_0_g128_enabled)` at :870 which skips the span check and llama_remap_q2_0_g128 entirely. Nothing on the false branch rejects id-43 tensors. gguf_init has already validated their spans against ggml_row_size(43) = 34 B / 128, which a turbo2_0 file matches exactly. So the file parses clean and our plain-scaled g128 kernel runs on rotated data. NOT TRIGGERED today, verified three ways at this head: no LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TURBO2_0 in include/llama.h, no TURBO target in tools/quantize/quantize.cpp, no TURBO entry in gguf-py/gguf/constants.py. SENSITIVITY HALF, added r2 after checker finding F6 - three asserted ABSENCES are void as evidence until the query is shown able to HIT in those same files, so: all three paths exist and are non-trivial at that ref (1350 / 596 / 4973 lines), each one DOES carry the turbo family under its sibling names (LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_TQ3_1S = 43 in llama.h, a {\"TQ3_1S\", ...} row in quantize.cpp, TQ3_1S = 45 in constants.py), and `TURBO` is a live token elsewhere in the same tree (GGML_TYPE_TURBO2_0 = 43, GGML_OP_TURBO_WHT) - yet it returns ZERO in all three registries. The query can fire, the files are the right files, and the absence is real. Also, block_turbo2_0's in-source comment still reads '// 10 bytes total' while its static_assert computes 34 - contract section 1.1 warned about exactly those stale comments and it is still stale here. REGISTER DEFECT FLAGGED TO HQ, NOT FIXED HERE: this fork is registered TWICE - as this local_checkouts entry and as the `turboquant` git remote of the engine repo - and the two disagree. The sibling clone src/llama-cpp-turboquant is at a33ef00b1 (2026-06-23) with origin/feature/turboquant-kv-cache at fca3093c9, both OLDER than the remote head this pin now names. One of the two should be authoritative. Full review: research/local-inference/2026-08-17-fork-delta-review.md",
