etal/SYCL/HIP: NOT dropped, escalated to HQ, because the rig has no such device and the F-107 and backend-ops proofs are therefore unobtainable. ~20 further CAPABILITY rows were NOT attempted this wave - each keeps its verdict, its evidence cell and an explicit outcome in research/local-inference/2026-08-18-turboquant-disposition.md, which carries all 183 rows and is regenerable by classify.py + coverage.py + disposition.py. PROOFS: build green by exe mtime; test-backend-ops 26213/26260 identical to the banked baseline and compared CASE-FOR-CASE (3 in / 3 out, all inside the two runbook-named flaky bands); arifi_sync_check.py GREEN, and shown RED on a planted violation. PIN HONESTY, recorded rather than smoothed over: while this lane ran, the live checkout advanced again to d14e36827. The pin records the sha I ACTUALLY REVIEWED (7ebcbb0b6), so currency will read BEHIND by exactly 3 fork-authored commits - 730cc87ed (moe-cache: heat-protected eviction keeps hot experts resident), cef75bf06 (docs split of the THROTTLE rule) and d14e36827 (docs: AI-assisted contribution workflows). Re-pinning past unreviewed commits to clear the row is the exact thing the gate exists to stop, and UPDATE-RUNBOOK 3 says so: UNKNOWN means leave BEHIND and say so. Live-head fork-authored total for the next lane: 186. HQ RULING 2026-08-18, EXECUTED: the 12 off-rig rows are LANDED UNBUILT (engine b5076671) rather than held - aa606e4a9, 78104ec46, f31e9b7c7, fa7393cd8, 2603f5d98, abbe07788, 7a2b25a0c, 1f8ceb051, 7b4192ad7, f050a2501, a577aebfb, ccd29136c. STATUS IS BUILD-UNPROVEN: this rig has no CUDA/Metal/SYCL/HIP device, so no F-107 exe proof and no backend-ops execution proof exists for any of them, and none is claimed. They cannot reach the rig build - CMakeCache has those six backends BOOL=OFF and build.ninja has zero compiling references to their directories - and the rig build plus arifi_sync_check.py are GREEN after landing, which proves only that they touch nothing here. Landed by taking the seven off-rig FILES at tip state. REASON OF RECORD: byte-identity with the fork on backends this estate cannot build - it removes drift instead of accumulating it. CORRECTION (lane-154 checker F1): an earlier version of this review justified it by 12/12 commits failing to apply as deltas. The checker re-derived 3 of 12 applying CLEANLY; I re-ran it two ways (their per-commit method against a fresh index at 0347ab14a, and an in-order sequential replay) and got 12/12 conflict both times and cannot reproduce their result. THE DISAGREEMENT IS UNRESOLVED, so that count is NO LONGER the justification - do not quote it. The over-reach is a declared superset and was measured directly: zero of our own rocmfp/tq3/turbo markers are deleted. OWED: ~30 min of a future lane with the hardware to verify them."
